.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1u2vpc/TASK-260715-1u2vpc_spawn-log_-tester--tester--codex-_RUN-260811-d6c00d.log:18185:- FINDING: SwiftNIO SSH hardcodes each child receive-window target to 16 MiB and exposes client `_rekey()` only internally. libssh2 exposes generic per-channel initial/remaining/adjust APIs, but its direct-tcpip helper fixes the 2 MiB default and it likewise has no public client-rekey API or automatic byte/time threshold.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1u2vpc/TASK-260715-1u2vpc_spawn-log_-tester--tester--codex-_RUN-260811-d6c00d.log:18186:- DECISION: ADR-014 remains open. Both candidates retain identical host-key, window, sustained 5 GiB rekey, scale (through 1,000 channels), cancellation, algorithm, extension-build, memory, and physical-size gates. Unknowns are named experiments in `.research/260720_task-260715-28ok1k-ssh-engine-candidate-audit.md`; no missing capability was waived.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-1a2cc4.log:981:- Closed the automatic client-rekey evidence gaps with deterministic protected-byte and injected-monotonic-time threshold tests. Each test reaches the production libssh2 KEX path under an open channel, asserts typed trigger/success events and the matching `clientByteRekeys` or `clientTimeRekeys` counter, proves post-KEX traffic, and restores sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, custom allocations, and buffers to zero after cancel/close.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-1a2cc4.log:982:- Recorded the test-design finding that a full-duplex echo can legitimately cross a per-direction protected-byte threshold in both directions. The final byte-threshold fixture uses bounded one-directional exec/stdin traffic so one exact trigger is reproducible without masking a valid second KEX.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-1a2cc4.log:1554:Implement the libssh2 CANDIDATE adapter — a SSHTransport implementation satisfying the candidate-neutral contract (TASK-260720-100wu6 in Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift), backed by libssh2. Package libssh2 (pinned per TASK-260715-28ok1k: commit a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719, BSD-3-Clause; OpenSSL 3.5.7 backend, Apache-2.0) as a static XCFramework binaryTarget via the TASK-260715-1g9cyt native seam + rebuild hook (checksum-verify pinned source; ADR-019). Live behind the ReluxTunnelCore SSHTransport boundary as a NAMED adapter module (libssh2/OpenSSL imported ONLY here; NOT in ReluxTunnelCore proper — make validate-core enforces). KEY FIT (why libssh2 suits the neutral seam where NIOSSH did not): drive libssh2 over the injected neutral SSHTCPConnection (readySome/readSome/writeSome/close) using libssh2 CUSTOM TRANSPORT send/recv callbacks (libssh2_session_callback_set) in NONBLOCKING mode (EAGAIN) — no socket/descriptor ownership needed, so the injected/fakeable connector (E-INJECTION) works. IMPLEMENT the full contract: connect + MANDATORY pre-auth host-key verification (libssh2 hostkey + SHA256 fingerprint to injected policy before credential lookup; changed-key stop); public-key auth via an EXTERNAL SIGNER (libssh2_userauth_publickey sign-callback — private key NEVER exported, stays with the caller); openDirectTCPIP (libssh2_channel_direct_tcpip_ex); openExecChannel (exec); upload via exec-stdin (NO SFTP); PER-CHANNEL window via libssh2_channel_open_ex(window_size)+window_read_ex+receive_window_adjust2 with CONSUMER-DRIVEN credit (return credit only after the API read consumes bytes — libssh2 lets the adapter own credit return, satisfying contract section 9 backpressure and maximumBufferedReadBytes); client REKEY by byte/time threshold scheduled by the adapter (libssh2 has no auto-rekey threshold — see audit); keepalive (libssh2_keepalive) with RTT; bounded IO/EOF/reset/cancel/close; error taxonomy; privacy-safe metrics; report exact negotiated KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC. UNIT-TEST driven over an in-memory/loopback byte seam (no live SSH fixtures — those are 39xz9g; cross-engine conformance is 2d3g5e; functional/scale is 1u2vpc, P0-gated). This is a CANDIDATE, not the selection (1gjxer). Build+test via swift build/test on macOS. If a contract clause genuinely cannot be satisfied by libssh2 public API, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact gap (that would signal a contract revision, a bigger decision) — do not force-fit.
