.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-4c1d55.log:6944:.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1af33i/TASK-260715-1af33i_inputs.md:1:Implement the ReluxNIOSSH CANDIDATE adapter — a SSHTransport implementation satisfying the TASK-260715-2ny6z4 conformance contract, backed by the ReluxNIOSSH fork (TASK-260715-nzdzv3, which exposes per-channel window control [contract section 9] and client-initiated byte/time rekey [section 10]). Live behind the ReluxTunnelCore SSHTransport boundary (TASK-260715-2nfz7w) as a NAMED adapter module (NIOSSH imported ONLY here, ADR-019 source dep); do NOT pull NIOSSH into ReluxTunnelCore proper (preserve check-core-boundaries). IMPLEMENT the full contract: connect + MANDATORY pre-auth host-key verification (raw key bytes + algorithm + SHA256 fingerprint to injected policy BEFORE credential lookup; changed-key stop per security-privacy.md); openDirectTCPIP; openExecChannel; upload via exec-stdin (NO SFTP); per-channel window (settable initial + observable remaining + cap via the fork API); client rekey by byte/time threshold (fork API); keepalive; bounded read/write/EOF/reset/cancel/close; error taxonomy; privacy-safe metrics. UNIT-TEST with NIOSSH in-memory/embedded channel harness (or lightweight local loopback) — do NOT require live SSH fixtures here (those are TASK-260715-39xz9g; cross-engine conformance is 2d3g5e; functional/rekey/scale matrix is 3ikonq, gated on P0). This is a CANDIDATE, not the selection (1gjxer selects); keep the engine injectable behind the boundary. Build + test via swift build / swift test on macOS. If the fork API is insufficient for a contract clause, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact gap (route back to nzdzv3); do not work around it.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-4c1d55.log:6959:.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_inputs.md:1:Implement the libssh2 CANDIDATE adapter — a SSHTransport implementation satisfying the candidate-neutral contract (TASK-260720-100wu6 in Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift), backed by libssh2. Package libssh2 (pinned per TASK-260715-28ok1k: commit a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719, BSD-3-Clause; OpenSSL 3.5.7 backend, Apache-2.0) as a static XCFramework binaryTarget via the TASK-260715-1g9cyt native seam + rebuild hook (checksum-verify pinned source; ADR-019). Live behind the ReluxTunnelCore SSHTransport boundary as a NAMED adapter module (libssh2/OpenSSL imported ONLY here; NOT in ReluxTunnelCore proper — make validate-core enforces). KEY FIT (why libssh2 suits the neutral seam where NIOSSH did not): drive libssh2 over the injected neutral SSHTCPConnection (readySome/readSome/writeSome/close) using libssh2 CUSTOM TRANSPORT send/recv callbacks (libssh2_session_callback_set) in NONBLOCKING mode (EAGAIN) — no socket/descriptor ownership needed, so the injected/fakeable connector (E-INJECTION) works. IMPLEMENT the full contract: connect + MANDATORY pre-auth host-key verification (libssh2 hostkey + SHA256 fingerprint to injected policy before credential lookup; changed-key stop); public-key auth via an EXTERNAL SIGNER (libssh2_userauth_publickey sign-callback — private key NEVER exported, stays with the caller); openDirectTCPIP (libssh2_channel_direct_tcpip_ex); openExecChannel (exec); upload via exec-stdin (NO SFTP); PER-CHANNEL window via libssh2_channel_open_ex(window_size)+window_read_ex+receive_window_adjust2 with CONSUMER-DRIVEN credit (return credit only after the API read consumes bytes — libssh2 lets the adapter own credit return, satisfying contract section 9 backpressure and maximumBufferedReadBytes); client REKEY by byte/time threshold scheduled by the adapter (libssh2 has no auto-rekey threshold — see audit); keepalive (libssh2_keepalive) with RTT; bounded IO/EOF/reset/cancel/close; error taxonomy; privacy-safe metrics; report exact negotiated KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC. UNIT-TEST driven over an in-memory/loopback byte seam (no live SSH fixtures — those are 39xz9g; cross-engine conformance is 2d3g5e; functional/scale is 1u2vpc, P0-gated). This is a CANDIDATE, not the selection (1gjxer). Build+test via swift build/test on macOS. If a contract clause genuinely cannot be satisfied by libssh2 public API, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact gap (that would signal a contract revision, a bigger decision) — do not force-fit.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-4c1d55.log:6984:.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-2ny6z4/TASK-260715-2ny6z4_inputs.md:1:Record the SSHTransport CONFORMANCE contract that BOTH engine adapters (ReluxNIOSSH fork via TASK-260715-nzdzv3; libssh2 via 1af33i/1ozsb6) must satisfy so they are interchangeable behind the ReluxTunnelCore SSHTransport boundary (TASK-260715-2nfz7w). INPUTS: TASK-260715-28ok1k audit — SwiftNIO SSH has NO public per-channel window setter/observer (16 MiB internal target) and _rekey() is internal (fork must expose both); libssh2 exposes per-channel windows publicly (channel_open_ex / window_read_ex / receive_window_adjust2) but has NO client-initiated rekey threshold (adapter must schedule rekey manually); NIOSSH has no RSA host keys, libssh2 has RSA-SHA2. .spec/ssh-transport.md, ADR-005 (direct-tcpip + exec), ADR-006 (exec-stdin upload, NO SFTP), ADR-014 (selection OPEN). DELIVER the conformance contract: connect + MANDATORY host-key verification before user auth (ed25519/ecdsa/rsa fingerprint + changed-key stop policy per security-privacy.md); openDirectTCPIP; openExecChannel; upload via exec-stdin; PER-CHANNEL WINDOW interface (settable initial window, observable remaining, explicit cap — required of BOTH adapters; matches audit E-WINDOW); REKEY interface (client-initiated by byte/time threshold — required of BOTH); keepalive; channel close/cancel/error semantics; concurrency expectation (hundreds..1000 channels). Define the conformance TEST MATRIX both adapters run (audit E-ALGO/E-HOSTAUTH/E-CHANNELS/E-SCALE/E-WINDOW/E-REKEY) so TASK-260715-2d3g5e implements ONE suite against BOTH. Keep the engine INJECTABLE; do NOT select it (that is 1gjxer). Contract doc only.
