.task-board/.resources/TASK-260728-yx2fca/TASK-260728-yx2fca_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-_RUN-260809-7d007e.log:12725:- REGRESSION (same source): a 220-character symmetric negation window let a neighbouring clause's negation launder an authorization — "`works.relux.proxy` is **migrated**" passed because AC4's earlier "explicitly **NOT** authorized" sat inside the window. A window wide enough to reach back over a list of four App IDs is necessarily wide enough to do this. Negation is now attributed **per clause**; clause splitting on `[.;:]\s+` and `,\s+(and|but|nor)\s+` is dot-safe because a dot *inside* these identifiers is never followed by whitespace. `negationWindow` was **removed**, not left as a field the gate reads and ignores — a dead field a gate still consults is the rot R32's dead-exclusion check exists to catch.
