.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-9a7468.log:2274:Implement the libssh2 CANDIDATE adapter — a SSHTransport implementation satisfying the candidate-neutral contract (TASK-260720-100wu6 in Sources/ReluxTunnelCore/SSHContracts.swift), backed by libssh2. Package libssh2 (pinned per TASK-260715-28ok1k: commit a34302491c164d53c900fec9b3cbb050ecebe719, BSD-3-Clause; OpenSSL 3.5.7 backend, Apache-2.0) as a static XCFramework binaryTarget via the TASK-260715-1g9cyt native seam + rebuild hook (checksum-verify pinned source; ADR-019). Live behind the ReluxTunnelCore SSHTransport boundary as a NAMED adapter module (libssh2/OpenSSL imported ONLY here; NOT in ReluxTunnelCore proper — make validate-core enforces). KEY FIT (why libssh2 suits the neutral seam where NIOSSH did not): drive libssh2 over the injected neutral SSHTCPConnection (readySome/readSome/writeSome/close) using libssh2 CUSTOM TRANSPORT send/recv callbacks (libssh2_session_callback_set) in NONBLOCKING mode (EAGAIN) — no socket/descriptor ownership needed, so the injected/fakeable connector (E-INJECTION) works. IMPLEMENT the full contract: connect + MANDATORY pre-auth host-key verification (libssh2 hostkey + SHA256 fingerprint to injected policy before credential lookup; changed-key stop); public-key auth via an EXTERNAL SIGNER (libssh2_userauth_publickey sign-callback — private key NEVER exported, stays with the caller); openDirectTCPIP (libssh2_channel_direct_tcpip_ex); openExecChannel (exec); upload via exec-stdin (NO SFTP); PER-CHANNEL window via libssh2_channel_open_ex(window_size)+window_read_ex+receive_window_adjust2 with CONSUMER-DRIVEN credit (return credit only after the API read consumes bytes — libssh2 lets the adapter own credit return, satisfying contract section 9 backpressure and maximumBufferedReadBytes); client REKEY by byte/time threshold scheduled by the adapter (libssh2 has no auto-rekey threshold — see audit); keepalive (libssh2_keepalive) with RTT; bounded IO/EOF/reset/cancel/close; error taxonomy; privacy-safe metrics; report exact negotiated KEX/host-key/cipher/MAC. UNIT-TEST driven over an in-memory/loopback byte seam (no live SSH fixtures — those are 39xz9g; cross-engine conformance is 2d3g5e; functional/scale is 1u2vpc, P0-gated). This is a CANDIDATE, not the selection (1gjxer). Build+test via swift build/test on macOS. If a contract clause genuinely cannot be satisfied by libssh2 public API, STOP-THE-LINE with the exact gap (that would signal a contract revision, a bigger decision) — do not force-fit.
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/TASK-260715-1ozsb6_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-_RUN-260810-9a7468.log:9228:.spec/decisions.md:28:| ADR-023 | Accepted | Scope the M0 SSH transport contract to **viability** (Option A). M0-viability-mandatory: pre-auth raw host-key evidence, approved public-key authentication, `direct-tcpip`, bidirectional exec plus exec/stdin relay upload, client-initiated rekey by byte/time threshold, bounded buffers and backpressure, deterministic cancellation and lifecycle, keepalive, privacy-safe errors, and cheaply-available metrics. Deferred to M3 as explicitly evidence-gated obligations, never silent waivers: (1) consumer-driven receive-window credit with an immutable per-channel cap, (2) the RFC 4254 channel-open rejection reason taxonomy, (3) exact exec-exit metadata distinguishing `status(0)` from `notReported` and exposing `coreDumped`, (4) deep rekey and keepalive observability including server-initiated KEX lifecycle/generation and reply-correlated keepalive RTT/timeout/miss. M0 adapters MUST surface deferred semantics as explicit not-reported/unsupported states. Owner tasks: `TASK-260728-yx2fca` (contract re-scope), `TASK-260728-3cveay` (M3 delivery). Resolves the three-round `TASK-260715-1ozsb6` stop-the-line. |
