   177	## Residual risks and revalidation triggers
   178	
   179	Residual risks: the selected libssh2 pin is untagged; static OpenSSL increases
   180	native attack surface, rebuild burden, and possible duplicate-crypto footprint;
   181	libssh2 session/channel lookup is mutable and partly O(n); OpenSSL allocations
   182	are outside libssh2 custom allocator accounting; issue #2023 remains unresolved;
   183	exact deep semantics and physical scale/footprint are still M3 gates; the
   184	controlled direct-tcpip row is a whole-cycle envelope rather than open-only
   185	latency; real-host reachability evidence and local candidate execution are
   186	separate privacy-safe facts.
   187	
   188	Reopen ADR-014 and route to analysis or the retained candidate if any of these
   189	occurs:
   190	
   191	- a mandatory selected-engine row becomes red, leaks a resource, loses or
   192	  corrupts traffic, violates host-before-auth, exports secret material, or
   193	  requires a weakened threshold;
   194	- a new libssh2/OpenSSL advisory affects the pin, issue #2023 is confirmed
   195	  against the selected algorithms, or a signed release changes relevant code;
   196	- the patch exceeds one allowlisted patch/six paths, changes crypto/algorithms,
   197	  exports private headers, or cannot rebase cleanly;
   198	- macOS/Xcode/deployment targets, OpenSSH server policy, approved algorithms,
   199	  real relux host policy, Keychain boundary, or adapter/core boundary changes;
   200	- M3 physical scale, memory, soak, DNS, or deep-observability evidence is red;
   201	- new evidence makes ReluxNIOSSH conform at materially lower security,
   202	  maintenance, or footprint cost.
   203	
